.TH AYAME-SPELL 1 "" "ayame-spell 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ayame-spell \- fast, low-noise spell checker for code and prose
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ayame-spell
.RI [ OPTIONS ]\ [ PATH ...]
.br
.B ayame-spell
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ayame-spell checks English and Japanese text in source trees and prose.
With no command it checks the supplied paths, or the current directory.
.SH COMMAND HELP
.SS ayame-spell
.nf
Fast, low-noise spell checker for code and prose — English & Japanese.
Running with no subcommand checks the given paths (default: current directory).

Usage: ayame-spell [OPTIONS] [PATH]... [COMMAND]

Commands:
  check        Check files and report issues (the default)
  fix          Apply all safe fixes in place (single-candidate corrections and mechanical notation
               conversions)
  words        Word management: bulk collection, triage, and dictionary additions
  dict         Shared dictionaries from the ayame-spell registry
  init         Write a starter ayame-spell.toml in the current directory
  config       Print the effective merged configuration
  completions  Generate a shell completion script on standard output
  lsp          Run the LSP server (used by editor integrations)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          Files or directories to check

Options:
  -w, --write
          Apply safe fixes in place (shorthand for `fix`)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, brief, json]

  -j, --threads <THREADS>
          Worker threads (default: number of CPUs)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
.fi
.SS ayame-spell check
.nf
Check files and report issues (the default)

Usage: ayame-spell check [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...

Options:
  -w, --write              Apply safe fixes in place
      --format <FORMAT>    [default: human] [possible values: human, brief, json]
  -j, --threads <THREADS>
  -h, --help               Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell fix
.nf
Apply all safe fixes in place (single-candidate corrections and mechanical notation conversions)

Usage: ayame-spell fix [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...

Options:
  -j, --threads <THREADS>
  -h, --help               Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell words
.nf
Word management: bulk collection, triage, and dictionary additions

Usage: ayame-spell words <COMMAND>

Commands:
  collect  Collect flagged words across files, ranked by frequency
  add      Add words to the project (default) or global word file
  triage   Interactive bulk triage of flagged words: multi-select what goes to the project
           dictionary, the global dictionary, or the ignore list
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell words collect
.nf
Collect flagged words across files, ranked by frequency

Usage: ayame-spell words collect [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...

Options:
      --min-count <MIN_COUNT>  Only include words flagged at least this many times [default: 1]
      --plain                  Print bare words only (ready to append to a word file)
      --json
  -h, --help                   Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell words add
.nf
Add words to the project (default) or global word file

Usage: ayame-spell words add [OPTIONS] <WORDS>...

Arguments:
  <WORDS>...

Options:
      --global
  -h, --help    Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell words triage
.nf
Interactive bulk triage of flagged words: multi-select what goes to the project dictionary, the
global dictionary, or the ignore list

Usage: ayame-spell words triage [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell dict
.nf
Shared dictionaries from the ayame-spell registry

Usage: ayame-spell dict <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list    List available dictionaries and their install status
  add     Download dictionaries and enable them in the project config
  remove  Delete a cached dictionary and disable it in the project config
  update  Re-download every cached dictionary from the registry
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell dict list
.nf
List available dictionaries and their install status

Usage: ayame-spell dict list

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell dict add
.nf
Download dictionaries and enable them in the project config

Usage: ayame-spell dict add [OPTIONS] <NAMES>...

Arguments:
  <NAMES>...

Options:
      --cache-only  Download to the cache only; leave the project config untouched
  -h, --help        Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell dict remove
.nf
Delete a cached dictionary and disable it in the project config

Usage: ayame-spell dict remove <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell dict update
.nf
Re-download every cached dictionary from the registry

Usage: ayame-spell dict update

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell init
.nf
Write a starter ayame-spell.toml in the current directory

Usage: ayame-spell init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --force  Overwrite an existing config file
  -h, --help   Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell config
.nf
Print the effective merged configuration

Usage: ayame-spell config

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell completions
.nf
Generate a shell completion script on standard output

Usage: ayame-spell completions <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
.fi
.SS ayame-spell lsp
.nf
Run the LSP server (used by editor integrations)

Usage: ayame-spell lsp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --stdio  Use standard input/output transport. Accepted for client compatibility; stdio is
               always the transport
  -h, --help   Print help
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ayame-spell.toml
Project configuration.
.TP
.I ayame-words.txt
Project word list used by the default configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means no findings, 1 means findings were reported, and 2 means an error occurred.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
https://hjosugi.github.io/ayame-spell/
